## TokenLighten MCP (compact)

Tools: `tl_read_file`, `tl_edit_file`, `tl_search_files`; use for all workspace read/search/edit. First lookup: `tl_read_file {"cwd":"<workspace>","query":"<entire user request, verbatim>","task":{"epoch":"new"}}` before native/Explore; unknown path omit `targets`. Use native tools if requested, TL is unavailable/bypassed, or its result is unusable or scope incomplete/absent; return to TL when usable. Search: `action:"find",queries:["<one identifier, literal>"]`, never a phrase; `action:"tree"` lists files; `scope.path`=known subtree, else repo-wide. CSS/literals: `action:"find"` (references: language symbols only).
Each call: top-level `cwd` (no pwd; else `cwd-required-for-edit`); add no `cwd` to a `next`. Working alone, omit `lane`. In parallel, set it on call 1 and never change it. Same request: latest `task.id` exactly→`task.handle`; never `epoch:"new"`; `expected_state_version` only with handle. User-declared read-only=`task.profile:"answer"`, change=`"generic"`; otherwise omit, never infer hints. Single edit: prepared `handle/search/replace`, `precondition:"unique-match"`, `allowPathFallback:false`; else ONE `tl_edit_file` `edits[]`. Handle must cover search; multiple windows: use `path/search/replace`+`precondition:"unique-match"`.
Unknown `kind`=SAFE-STOP: report; no edit/field inference. Follow `decision.kind`; `act.answer`/`act.edit` ends discovery after same-batch replies settle. `decision.next[]`: all calls in one tool-call turn, verbatim. Same-task/batch act supersedes sibling `discover.next` only absent refusal/unknown; refusal→`retry` only; unknown stops. Trace branch/loop guards; definitions/comments/calculation/logging ≠ execution; Trace all arg identities/copies; unknown bodies limit claims; names ≠ behavior. `evidence[].body` is exact source; use it without rereading. If required body is missing after `act.answer`, read that target. Batch independent reads. Later reads=`targets:[{path|handle,range}]`, no `query`; docs=`select.sections`. `next` whole call, verbatim; hints advisory. Lost context: same call with `task.force_serve:true`. `read.receipt`: follow `next` if present; else act or stop on restated evidence/certificate.
New files/tests=`edits:[{path,create:true,content}]`+explicit `cwd`; empty frontier+`create_target`=create. Edit served bytes only. `edit.applied`=landed; `edit.rolled_back`=nothing landed; `edit.state_unknown`=>`recovery` first. Never retry failed edit verbatim (`operation_id` replay safe). Use returned verification kit; no closure pull just for it. Follow returned closure `next`/`verification.next_call` + nonempty `recipe.gaps`; run `toolchain.test_entry` from `toolchain.test_entry_dir`.
Batch ready fixes/tests/style across stages in ONE `tl_edit_file` `edits[]`; verify. Repair unfinished requested work from related failures; retest. Stop on relevant pass; no extra harnesses, before/after builds, warning/style edits; report unrelated/pre-existing failures.
Use shell for build/tests/git; use native read/search/edit only under the fallback conditions above.
